      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{59a50e29df83a3566e6fb959|full_name}: Let me explain, why has manual added information about the Physics Sync? Then manual should also explain by removing VRC Object Sync, it will not share position and rotation.\nAccording the manual, it looks like you need also VRC Object Sync for pickup items even it must done locally? Why is parameter there then?\nIf the parameter was actually not needed, they should remove it from the manual. VRChat dev should update the manual to match with current version.\nThen remove component VRC Object Sync will make pickup locally, right?\nAlso, if you have Udon Behaviour on, it will show warning you need VRC Object Sync - even you want keep it locally. It's not very clear here what is needed or not for local pickup. The manual right now seems tell you, you need it because it has parameter to disable sync. But it's not even added in current version. De manual doesn't match with current version yet.",
